26. API structure for Angular
Your Angular developer can now work with:

List
GET /api/penalties

Example:

GET /api/penalties?page=1&limit=20

Search
GET /api/penalties?search=Rahul

Recovery type
GET /api/penalties?recovery_type=loans

Employee
GET /api/penalties?employee_id=15

Month/year
GET /api/penalties?month=8&year=2026

Single record
GET /api/penalties/101

Create
POST /api/penalties

Body:

{
    "employee_id": 15,
    "penalty_date": "2026-08-01",
    "recovery_type": "loans",
    "particulars": "Personal Loan",
    "amount": 100000,
    "show_cause_issued": false,
    "explanation_heard_in_presence": null,
    "number_of_installments": 10,
    "first_month": 8,
    "first_year": 2026,
    "last_month": 5,
    "last_year": 2027,
    "date_of_complete_recovery": null,
    "remarks": "Approved by HR"
}

27. Update API
PUT /api/penalties/101

Body:

{
    "amount": 120000,
    "remarks": "Amount corrected by HR"
}

Database:

amount = 120000

but:

calculation_amount = 100000

So payroll remains:

100000

28. Export API
GET /api/penalties/export

With filters:

GET /api/penalties/export?recovery_type=loans&year=2026

The Excel export approach above follows Laravel Excel's standard Excel::download() flow. 
L
Laravel Excel
+1

29. Bulk Excel upload
POST /api/penalties/bulk-upload

Multipart form-data:

file = penalties.xlsx

Angular sends:

const formData = new FormData();
formData.append('file', file);

this.http.post(
    '/api/penalties/bulk-upload',
    formData
);

30. I would make one additional API
For Angular, give the frontend the allowed recovery types.

Create:

GET /api/penalties/recovery-types

In controller:

public function recoveryTypes()
{
    return response()->json([
        'status' => 200,
        'data' => [
            [
                'value' => 'damage',
                'label' => 'Damage',
            ],
            [
                'value' => 'loss',
                'label' => 'Loss',
            ],
            [
                'value' => 'fine',
                'label' => 'Fine',
            ],
            [
                'value' => 'advance',
                'label' => 'Advance',
            ],
            [
                'value' => 'loans',
                'label' => 'Loans',
            ],
